      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Since $VWX$ is a right triangle, we can use the definition of the tangent function to find $\\tan V$.\n\nThe tangent of an angle in a right triangle is defined as the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the side adjacent to the angle.\n\nIn this case, the side opposite angle $V$ is $WX$ and the side adjacent to angle $V$ is $VW$.\n\nSo, $\\tan V = \\frac{WX}{VW}$.\n\nWe can find $WX$ using the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$WX^2 = VW^2 + VW^2$\n\n$WX^2 = 3^2 + 3^2$\n\n$WX^2 = 9 + 9$\n\n$WX^2 = 18$\n\n$WX = \\sqrt{18} = 3\\sqrt{2}$\n\nNow we can substitute the values into the tangent formula:\n\n$\\tan V = \\frac{WX}{VW} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{3} = \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}}$\n\nThe answer is: \\sqrt{2}",
